# 低频词汇 List01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List01核心词汇

abide /əˈbaɪd/ v. 遵守 Citizens must abide by the law. 公民必须遵守法律。
abstain /əbˈsteɪn/ v. 弃权 Two members abstained from the vote. 两名成员弃权。
acclaim /əˈkleɪm/ n./v. 赞誉 The novel received widespread acclaim. 这部小说获得了广泛赞誉。
acquaint /əˈkweɪnt/ v. 使了解 The orientation program acquaints new staff with the rules. 入职培训让新员工了解规则。
adhere /ədˈhɪə(r)/ v. 遵守 All participants must adhere to the guidelines. 所有参与者必须遵守准则。
adjacent /əˈdʒeɪsnt/ adj. 毗邻的 The hotel is adjacent to the train station. 酒店毗邻火车站。
advent /ˈædvent/ n. 到来 The advent of AI has transformed many industries. 人工智能的到来改变了许多行业。
affirm /əˈfɜːm/ v. 确认 The court affirmed the original ruling. 法院确认了原裁决。
aggregate /ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt/ v./adj. 合计 The aggregate cost of the project exceeded the budget. 项目的总成本超出了预算。
allegiance /əˈliːdʒəns/ n. 忠诚 The soldiers swore allegiance to the country. 士兵们宣誓效忠国家。
alliance /əˈlaɪəns/ n. 联盟 The two companies formed a strategic alliance. 两家公司结成了战略联盟。
allot /əˈlɒt/ v. 分配 The funds were allotted to various projects. 资金被分配给了各个项目。
amid /əˈmɪd/ prep. 在…之中 The policy was adopted amid controversy. 该政策在争议中被采纳。
annex /əˈneks/ v. 兼并 The territory was annexed after the war. 战后该领土被兼并。
array /əˈreɪi/ n. 一系列 The system offers an array of features. 该系统提供了一系列功能。
ascertain /ˌæsəˈteɪn/ v. 查明 The committee sought to ascertain the facts. 委员会试图查明事实。
aspiration /ˌæspəˈreɪʃn/ n. 抱负 Young people have high aspirations for the future. 年轻人对未来有很高的抱负。
assent /əˈsent/ n./v. 同意 The proposal received royal assent. 该提案获得了皇家批准。
attorney /əˈtɜːni/ n. 律师 The attorney represented the defendant in court. 律师在法庭上为被告辩护。
augment /ɔːɡˈment/ v. 增加 The company augmented its workforce with temporary staff. 公司用临时员工增加了劳动力。
avert /əˈvɜːt/ v. 防止 Emergency measures averted a catastrophe. 紧急措施防止了一场灾难。
bail /beɪl/ n./v. 保释 The suspect was released on bail of $50,000. 嫌疑人以5万美元保释金获释。
benign /bɪˈnaɪn/ adj. 良性的 The policy had a benign effect on the economy. 该政策对经济产生了良性影响。
bizarre /bɪˈzɑː(r)/ adj. 古怪的 The incident had bizarre consequences. 该事件产生了古怪的后果。
blunt /blʌnt/ adj./v. 直率的 She was blunt in her assessment of the situation. 她对形势的评估很直率。
boast /bəʊst/ v. 夸耀 The city boasts several world-class museums. 该城市拥有几座世界级博物馆。
brace /breɪs/ v. 准备 The country braced for the economic impact. 该国为经济影响做好了准备。
brisk /brɪsk/ adj. 兴旺的 Trade has been brisk in the first quarter. 第一季度贸易一直很兴旺。
bulk /bʌlk/ n. 大量 The bulk of the evidence points to his innocence. 大量证据表明他是无辜的。
bypass /ˈbaɪpɑːs/ v. 绕过 They found a way to bypass the bureaucracy. 他们找到了一种绕过官僚主义的方法。
